## 9. Limitations

- Missing ratings were represented as zero in the baseline user-item matrix, which can influence similarity calculations.
- The evaluation covered 456 eligible users rather than all 943 users.
- The recommendation approaches used different prediction strategies and should be interpreted in the context of their implementations.
- SVD predictions were not constrained to the original 1–5 rating scale.
- The results are specific to the MovieLens dataset and the experimental configuration.

## 10. Conclusion

This project implemented and evaluated user-based collaborative filtering, item-based collaborative filtering and SVD matrix factorization for movie recommendation.

User-based collaborative filtering achieved the best Precision@10 of 35.61%, followed by SVD at 33.00%.

The experiment provided practical experience in recommendation systems, similarity computation, matrix factorization, personalised recommendations and model evaluation.

